--- body ---
## Context

0012 accepted. Replace the `Status:` header enum with a binary
closed/not-closed criterion. Decisions recorded in 0012's log:

- `Closed:` header is the canonical closure mechanism (in-place, no
  file move required); value is required non-empty.
- Path component test (not substring): a component equals `closed`,
  starts with `closed-`/`closed.`, or ends with `-closed`
  (case-insensitive). Covers `tickets/closed/`, `archive/closed/`,
  `0001-foo-closed.erg`; rules out `disclosed`, `enclosed`.
- `Closed:` detection is a line-start header-key match, not free
  substring; forbidden in log and body sections.
- `pending` is dropped entirely.
- Migration: `erg migrate` is the one command that tolerates `Status:`
  lines; all other commands reject them. No global install ordering
  required — install binary first, migrate repos at your pace.

## Actions

### A. `rules/tickets.md` spec change

- Remove `Status:` from the headers table.
- Add `Closed:` header row: optional, non-repeatable, preamble only;
  value carries reason (PR reference, supersession note, "abandoned —
  out of scope", etc.).
- Document the closed/not-closed criterion:
  > A ticket is **closed** if at least one holds:
  > 1. A path component (directory name or basename without extension)
  >    equals `closed`, starts with `closed-`/`closed.`, or ends with
  >    `-closed` (case-insensitive).
  > 2. A preamble line begins with `Closed:` (header-key match at line
  >    start; value required, non-empty).
  > Otherwise the ticket is **not-closed** (open).
- Document that `Closed:` is forbidden in log and body sections, and
  that an empty `Closed:` value is a validation error.
- Remove `pending` from all enum references.
- Update the example tickets in the spec accordingly.

### B. Validator (`tickets/tools/go/`)

- Remove `Status` from the known-headers set; reject it on sight
  **except** inside `erg migrate` (which is the one command that
  tolerates `Status:` lines in order to convert them).
- Add `Closed` as a known optional non-repeatable header, preamble-only;
  reject empty value.
- Detection: match `^Closed:` at line start (header-key position), not
  free substring. Enforce `Closed:` forbidden in log and body sections.
- Apply the closed/not-closed criterion: derive `Erg.Closed` from
  path component test OR preamble `Closed:` header.
- Path component test: a component equals `closed`, starts with
  `closed-`/`closed.`, or ends with `-closed` (case-insensitive).
- `erg ready` exclusion: use `Erg.Closed` (unchanged semantics,
  different source).

### C. `erg close` rewrite

Current behaviour: find `Status: open|doing` line, replace with
`Status: closed`.

New behaviour: append `Closed: <reason>` to the preamble (after last
existing header, before the blank line preceding `--- log ---`).
Requires non-empty reason (existing behaviour — `erg close` already
requires a reason argument). Does not touch any `Status:` line;
`erg validate` will reject stale `Status:` lines post-migration.

### D. `erg migrate` new subcommand

```
erg migrate [dir]
```

Idempotent. For every `.erg` file under `dir` (default: `tickets/`):

1. If preamble contains `Status: closed` (any case):
   - Remove the `Status:` line.
   - Append `Closed: migrated from Status: closed` to the preamble.
2. If preamble contains `Status: doing` or `Status: pending` or
   `Status: open` (any case):
   - Remove the `Status:` line. (Ticket becomes not-closed — correct.)
3. If no `Status:` line: no-op.

After processing all files, print a summary:
```
migrated: N tickets (K closed, M open/doing/pending stripped)
already clean: P tickets
```

Exit 0 always (migration is idempotent; running twice is safe).

Does NOT commit. User reviews the diff and commits manually.

### E. `erg update` integration

After a successful binary swap, `cmdUpdate` scans the ticket directory
(default: `tickets/`) for any file with a `Status:` line in its
preamble. If any found, automatically invoke `cmdMigrate` and print:

```
erg: updated (abc123 → def456)
erg: detected Status: headers in N tickets — running migrate...
migrated: N tickets (K closed, M open/doing/pending stripped)
Review with: git diff tickets/
Then commit: git commit -m "chore: migrate to Closed: header"
```

If no `Status:` lines found after update, print nothing extra (already
migrated or fresh install).

### F. Tests

- Validator rejects `Status:` header (any value).
- Validator accepts `Closed:` in preamble with non-empty value.
- Validator rejects `Closed:` with empty value.
- Validator rejects `Closed:` in log or body sections.
- Validator does not false-positive on `disclosed` or `enclosed` in path.
- `erg ready` excludes tickets with `Closed:` header.
- `erg ready` excludes tickets in a `closed/` path component.
- `erg ready` excludes tickets with `-closed.erg` basename suffix.
- `erg ready` does NOT exclude tickets with `disclosed` in path.
- `erg close` appends `Closed: <reason>` to preamble; no Status line.
- `erg close` rejects empty reason.
- `erg migrate`: `Status: closed` ticket → `Closed: migrated from Status: closed` added, `Status:` removed.
- `erg migrate`: open/doing/pending ticket → `Status:` removed, not closed.
- `erg migrate` idempotent: running twice produces same result.
- `erg migrate` tolerates `Status:` lines; `erg validate` rejects them.
- `erg update` auto-runs migrate when Status: lines detected post-update.
- `erg update` is silent about migration when already clean.
- All existing tests pass.

## Migration instructions (for README / release notes)

1. Build and install the new binary.
2. Run `erg migrate tickets/` in each repo (`erg migrate` tolerates
   `Status:` lines; all other commands reject them after this point).
3. Review the diff (`git diff tickets/`).
4. Commit: `git commit -m "chore: migrate to Closed: header (erg migrate)"`.
5. Verify: `erg validate tickets/` → PASS.

No global ordering hazard: install the binary first, then migrate repos
at your own pace. Until `erg migrate` runs in a repo, only `erg migrate`
will work on it — `erg validate`, `erg ready`, etc. will reject
`Status:` lines and exit non-zero.

## Out of scope

- Path convention for organizing closed tickets into subdirectories
  (left to each project; the path test makes any convention work).
- `erg archive` interaction (archive implies closed; no change needed —
  archive dir name contains `archive`, not `closed`, so path test
  doesn't fire; `Closed:` header in archived tickets is sufficient).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `rules/tickets.md` updated per §A
- [ ] Validator rejects `Status:`, accepts `Closed:` per §B
- [ ] `erg close` appends `Closed:` header per §C
- [ ] `erg migrate` converts all tickets atomically per §D
- [ ] `erg update` auto-invokes migrate when Status: lines detected per §E
- [ ] Tests cover all cases in §F
- [ ] `make test` and `make validate` green on this repo's own tickets
      (after running `erg migrate` on them)
- [ ] Migration instructions documented
